      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Right-sided arcus aorta (RSAA) is a rare congenital anomaly that may cause chronic cough and dyspnoea. We aimed to define RSAA as a new syndrome characterised by RSAA, dyspnoea and cough during exercise. RSAA syndrome should be included in the differential diagnosis of asthma."},
